<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Single-scene novel view synthesis results of the baselines on a sample scene from each environment.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Representation</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scene volume.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given depth maps provided with our dataset,
we partition the scene into a voxel grid <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and represent the space using an octree <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite>.
This allows for efficient memory utilization as the octree only represents voxels that contain a surface.
We use <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> to represent a collection of feature vectors over the feature volume.
Each voxel <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in the octree stores learnable feature embeddings <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{v,j}\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{v,j}\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> at each of its eight corners (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2,\dots 8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2,\dots 8\}</annotation></semantics></math>), where feature embeddings are shared between spatially adjacent voxels.
In other words, each vertex in the octree is associated with one feature embedding.
The feature embedding <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined for any point <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> in the space as <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{p}=\psi(p;\mathcal{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{p}=\psi(p;\mathcal{Z})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(.)</annotation></semantics></math> is the tri-linear interpolation between corner features of the voxel in which <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is contained.
The collection of feature embeddings <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is learned to encode local properties of each voxel, while the tri-linear interpolation and shared features between adjacent voxels ensure a degree of continuity in the feature space.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ray parameterization.</span>
Since we aim at learning voxel-based functions, we parameterize a given ray <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">r</span> in the local coordinates of each voxel.
Specifically, as shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.3 Environments ‣ 3 Ray-Traced Multi-View Dataset ‣ RTMV: A Ray-Traced Multi-View Synthetic Dataset for Novel View Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (a), we compute the intersection points <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},p_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},p_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> of <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">r</span> with the minimum bounding sphere around the voxel, define vectors <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from the voxel origin to these intersections, then scale them to unit norm: <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{i}=\hat{p}_{i}/\|\hat{p}_{i}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{i}=\hat{p}_{i}/\|\hat{p}_{i}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.
This gives us the overparameterized representation <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{r}=[\begin{matrix}\tilde{p}_{1}\,\,|\,\,\tilde{p}_{2}\end{matrix}]\in\mathbb{R}^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">r</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" lspace="0.618em">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{r}=[\begin{matrix}\tilde{p}_{1}\,\,|\,\,\tilde{p}_{2}\end{matrix}]\in\mathbb{R}^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Voxel-based light field function</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The collection <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is split into feature embeddings <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> for optical thickness, and feature embeddings <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> for color.
Each of these sub-collections has an associated small decoder network: <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> for optical thickness, and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> for color.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a voxel <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and a ray <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">r</span>, we first compute the ray-voxel intersection points <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.3 Environments ‣ 3 Ray-Traced Multi-View Dataset ‣ RTMV: A Ray-Traced Multi-View Synthetic Dataset for Novel View Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (b)) using an efficient ray-AABB intersection algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>.
We then estimate the optical thickness and color of the ray in two steps.
The first step estimates whether the ray hits a surface within <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, and produces an estimate for the location of the hit surface point <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> as a convex combination of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, we have:</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau,\eta=F^{\mathcal{T}}(\textbf{r},z^{\mathcal{T}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">r</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau,\eta=F^{\mathcal{T}}(\textbf{r},z^{\mathcal{T}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the estimated optical thickness,
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the mixing factor interpolating between <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
, and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\mathcal{T}}=[\begin{matrix}\psi(x_{1};\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{T}})\,\,|\,\,\psi(x_{2};\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{T}})\end{matrix}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\mathcal{T}}=[\begin{matrix}\psi(x_{1};\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{T}})\,\,|\,\,\psi(x_{2};\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{T}})\end{matrix}]</annotation></semantics></math> is the combined interpolated feature embedding at the two intersection points.
If <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the surface point <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated as <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{s}=\eta x_{1}+(1-\eta)x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{s}=\eta x_{1}+(1-\eta)x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> can be seen as a within-voxel depth.
Otherwise, if <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the ray does not hit any surface.
We estimate surface points to encourage continuous sampling of color features between adjacent voxels.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The second step samples color features <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> at the estimated surface point <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and computes the color value <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=F^{\mathcal{C}}(\textbf{r},z^{\mathcal{C}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">r</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=F^{\mathcal{C}}(\textbf{r},z^{\mathcal{C}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\mathcal{C}}=\psi(\hat{x}_{s};\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\mathcal{C}}=\psi(\hat{x}_{s};\mathcal{Z}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the interpolated feature embedding at <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.3 Environments ‣ 3 Ray-Traced Multi-View Dataset ‣ RTMV: A Ray-Traced Multi-View Synthetic Dataset for Novel View Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (c)).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Rendering</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To render a pixel from an SVLF, we perform volume rendering.
We first evaluate the color <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and optical thickness <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for all voxels intersected by the ray,
then we aggregate the color values using alpha compositing.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluating intersected voxels.</span>
We first compute a list of all voxels intersected by the ray.
We use the sparse ray-octree intersection algorithm of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite> that leverages the hierarchical octree structure and parallel scan kernels <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite> for accelerated computation.
This step yields <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for each intersected voxel.
We then evaluate the optical thickness <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and color <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> at each intersected voxel as described in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Voxel-based light field function ‣ 4 Sparse Voxel Light Field (SVLF) ‣ RTMV: A Ray-Traced Multi-View Synthetic Dataset for Novel View Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.
Each voxel is evaluated only once by querying two lightweight decoder networks <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and  <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> to compute the optical thickness and color, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Aggregating color values along the ray.</span>
We use alpha compositing to compute the ray color <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\textbf{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">r</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\textbf{r})</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\textbf{r})=\sum_{i=1}^{N}T_{v_{i}}(1-e^{-\tau_{v_{i}}})c_{v_{i}},\quad T_{v_{i}}=\prod_{j&lt;i}e^{-\tau_{v_{j}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">r</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\textbf{r})=\sum_{i=1}^{N}T_{v_{i}}(1-e^{-\tau_{v_{i}}})c_{v_{i}},\quad T_{v_{i}}=\prod_{j&lt;i}e^{-\tau_{v_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of intersected voxels, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{v_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{v_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transmittance up until voxel <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and voxels are indexed by the order of their intersection along the ray.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
